
# 2026-07-30 20:06:44.671723
+Resolve GitHub issue #1: clamp() returns the wrong value when input is above the range
+
+Issue description:
+`clamp(value, low, high)` in clamp.py is supposed to clamp `value` into `[low, high]`. When `value` is above `high`, it returns the wrong bound instead of the correct one. `test_clamp_above_range` in test_clamp.py currently fails because of this. Please fix clamp() so all tests pass.
+
+Make the minimal, correct code changes needed to resolve this issue. Do not modify unrelated files.

